1. The client reported that attendance data for Date: 08/07/24 & 14/07/24 & 16/07/24 & 17/07/24, is not showing in the attendance sheet. I opened the attendance record of the employee and found that the punches were not showing. I then went to the miscellaneous menu to check all the transactions for that day and found attendance transactions, but they were not showing in the attendance sheet. 
2. I accessed the Zydus server to check which flag is showing for the transactions on that particular date. 3. I opened the database and executed the following queries: SELECT * FROM empmaster WHERE code='124316'; 
SELECT * FROM attddetails WHERE empid='' AND attddate='2024/07/12'; 
4. I found an 'X' flag for 4 attendance punches, so I modified the process flag in SQL DBX and updated the flag to 'P'. 
5. I opened the attendance sheet, and now all the attendance data is showing properly.

solution:
1. The client reported that attendance data for Date: 08/07/24 & 14/07/24 & 16/07/24 & 17/07/24, is not showing in the attendance sheet. I opened the attendance record of the employee and found that the punches were not showing. I then went to the miscellaneous menu to check all the transactions for that day and found attendance transactions, but they were not showing in the attendance sheet. 
2. I accessed the Zydus server to check which flag is showing for the transactions on that particular date. 3. I opened the database and executed the following queries: SELECT * FROM empmaster WHERE code='124316'; 
SELECT * FROM attddetails WHERE empid='' AND attddate='2024/07/12'; 
4. I found an 'X' flag for 4 attendance punches, so I modified the process flag in SQL DBX and updated the flag to 'P'. 
5. I opened the attendance sheet, and now all the attendance data is showing properly.

